{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-3230"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Manufacture of sports goods"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "3230"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :sports-goods/manufacturing
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :materials-safety :consumer-protection]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :sports-goods-plant-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :cae]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies []
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "SportsGoodsAdvisor ⊣ Sports Goods Plant Operations Governor,
 langgraph-clj StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A sports-goods
 PLANT OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor for molding/assembly/finishing
 lines producing finished sports goods (balls/rackets/protective
 gear/fitness equipment) -- not direct molding/assembly-line-
 equipment control authority and not a product-safety-certification
 (e.g. impact-protection standard compliance) authority. Four ops
 (`:log-production-batch` / `:schedule-maintenance` /
 `:flag-safety-concern` / `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect
 :propose` only. Thirteen concrete governor checks elaborate this
 blueprint's four HARD invariants: propose-only effect, closed op
 allowlist, closed proposal-effect allowlist (no direct molding/
 assembly-line-equipment control), permanent equipment-actuate block,
 permanent product-safety-certification-authority block (this actor
 never self-issues an impact-protection/product-safety compliance
 certification), independent plant-equipment verification/
 registration before maintenance scheduling, independent batch
 verification/registration before shipment coordination, independent
 shipment-quantity recompute against the batch's own logged
 production quantity, double-schedule guard, product-type validation,
 impact-protection-rating plausibility validation, batch-weight
 plausibility validation, and defect-rate plausibility validation.
 Safety-concern flagging (materials-safety hazard, product-safety-
 standard/impact-protection-rating concern) ALWAYS escalates to a
 human plant supervisor; `:log-production-batch` is the only op
 eligible to auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when governor-clean."}
